    "volume": "The side camera independently traces the near liquid boundary against the front graduations. Each optical transfer is the measured change of liquid volume in the cup across a complete command or pulse train. A withdraws liquid and B returns it.",
    "optical_mean_ml_per_pulse": "Complete optically measured train volume divided by the acknowledged pulse count. Each exposure pair brackets the whole train.",
    "optical_full_cycle_ml_min": "Complete optically measured volume divided by the board-reported full cycle duration, converted to mL/min. A recurring pulse schedule includes the pause after the final gate.",
    "supported_load": "The scale supports the OXO cup, its contents and the forces the hoses exert on it. Tube movement can change the indicated load while the liquid level stays fixed.",
    "supported_load_change_g": "After minus before on the scale display. The directional_load_change_g column reverses this sign for an A withdrawal and retains it for a B return. A zero-drive control keeps the signed change in supported_load_change_g.",
    "gate_s": "Board-reported total duration of commanded on-windows. In the zero-duty controls the timed windows leave the motor off.",
    "train_s": "Board time between the first gate opening and final gate closing, including internal pauses.",
    "full_cycles_s": "Train time plus the final scheduled off interval.",
    "appliance_schedule": "Low, mid and full identify the pulse schedules at the appliance’s 1:20 setting. This rig measures undiluted concentrate between two vessels. Water flow and mixed beverage ratio require a water-channel measurement."
